at all (the old key predicate refused it as "neither test_only nor code_patch"), so the task type is detected from
night_meta.json's `task=…/tasks/doc_patch/` path AND checker.out's shape (a `PASS D0`/`FAIL D0` line, no `mode:` line,
no B0 line), which must agree. Every verdict sentence is the checker's OWN line (D0, D1, D2, D3, one D4 + one D5 per
required section, D6, D7 PASS/INFO, D8 PASS/INFO, D9 PASS/INFO, RESULT) and each is cross-checked against the artefact
it was counted from: the RESULT total against the input's defect_line (7 if must_remove else 6, +1 expected_plus, +1
insert_after — the checker's own formula), the D2 apply mode against apply_check.out / apply_check_lenient.out /
patch.reanchored.diff + apply_check_rean.out / patch.as-written.diff + patch.anchor_restored.diff + apply_check_ar.out,
patch.diff against the out.md fence (byte-equal unless D2 names a rewrite), before.md against input.json['files'] and
